  "findings": [
    "The enzyme/non-enzyme gap is positive at all three cutoffs tested (+0.43, +0.84, +0.34), so the direction of the result does not depend on the cutoff; only its size does.",
    "Ten angstroms is the conventional interface definition and also the best separation here. That coincidence is stated rather than leaned on.",
    "Spike RBD carries a 682 square angstrom contiguous hydrophobic patch against the main protease's 415, which is the macrocycle-relevant comparison and the opposite of what pocket depth would say."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Six structures, chosen to span the contrast, not sampled.",
    "The glycan term is weak as implemented: shielding is counted only near the single largest patch, so it fires on one or two sequons where the spike trimer carries sixteen in the chain. It is a floor on shielding, not a measure of it.",
    "One structure per target, with no conformational ensemble. A prefusion and postfusion glycoprotein present different surfaces and only one is scored.",
    "No validation against measured macrocycle binding, because no such labelled set exists."
  ],
